+
+### Declared source roles in selector context (S6 live-02 correction)
+
+The selector presentation distinguishes the existing `original.sources` and
+fulfillment `context.members` declarations from the wider observed `readRoots`.
+Their exact source bodies remain consumable in the prompt (or as exact ranges
+inside its original task). Every other observed file contributes its path,
+state, byte count and digest, plus existing admitted observations and current
+dependency correspondence. No filename heuristic or semantic F_D compression
+selects source material. An explicit source designation retains its body even
+when an otherwise identical file is an output. Inventory and producer reports
+confer no independent adequacy or completion.
+
+The complete authoritative task, physical context, input identity and raw
+response domains remain intact. Native work and independent assessment retain
+their separately declared complete subject bodies. The selector lane has no
+file tools, so required source content cannot be replaced by external locators.
+The 131,072-byte selected bound is unchanged; overflow remains an explicit
+refusal. Verification includes the actual post-Design fold, parent, expanded
+context and owned selector assembly, plus prospective assessment preparation
+over those retained assets. Controlled preparation is not an admitted UAT
+selection or semantic assessment.
